# The --skip-to-area row table (scripts/check_skip_targets.sh).
# One row per sub-area: every sub-area 1..N-1 of the 17 multi-area levels
# (38), each entered by one area-0 portal. A row passes when its run prints
# the skip's release line ("[skip-to-level] level playable") carrying every
# expect token, the level and area words (0x8006C5BC, 0x8006C5C8) read back
# from RAM at release: game.state 13 seen after the EnterSubArea call, then
# gameplay live in the target area. It fails when the run prints the
# fail-safe line. Level 31 arrives in the first-visit speech (game.state 1),
# which the area-0 portal refuses; its rows replay a movie that dismisses
# it. frames is the run's VBL limit (releases measured at VBL 1113, 1327
# for level 31).
#
# name | args                                                                                              | frames | expect
11_1   | --skip-to-area 11:1                                                                               | 2000   | level=11 area=1
11_2   | --skip-to-area 11:2                                                                               | 2000   | level=11 area=2
12_1   | --skip-to-area 12:1                                                                               | 2000   | level=12 area=1
12_2   | --skip-to-area 12:2                                                                               | 2000   | level=12 area=2
13_1   | --skip-to-area 13:1                                                                               | 2000   | level=13 area=1
13_2   | --skip-to-area 13:2                                                                               | 2000   | level=13 area=2
